ndefined/empty externalId). The result is always `undefined`, making the fallback non-functional. The same pattern exists in `deleteEvent` at line 317."}, {"file": "packages/features/bookings/lib/handleNewBooking.ts", "line": 1076, "severity": "high", "category": "bug", "title": "Team destination calendars silently dropped when organizer has no destination calendar", "body": "When neither `eventType.destinationCalendar` nor `organizerUser.destinationCalendar` exists, `evt.destinationCalendar` is set to `null`. The subsequent line `evt.destinationCalendar?.push(...teamDestinationCalendars)` uses optional chaining, so when `destinationCalendar` is `null`, the push is silently skipped and all team members' destination calendars are lost. This means collective events where the organizer has no calendar integration but team members do will fail to create calendar events for those team members."}, {"file": "packages/types/Calendar.d.ts", "line": 221, "severity": "medium", "category": "api", "title": "Calendar interface requires credentialId but multiple implementations do not accept it", "body": "The `Calendar` interface now declares `createEvent(event: CalendarEvent, credentialId: number)`, but `LarkCalendarService`, `Office365CalendarService`, and `BaseCalendarService` (CalDAV) all define `createEvent(event: CalendarEvent)` without the `credentialId` parameter. While TypeScript allows this (functions with fewer parameters are assignable to types expecting more), the `credentialId` is silently ignored by these implementations. If the intent is for all calendar services to use `credentialId` to select the correct destination calendar from the array, these services need to be updated."}, {"file": "packages/core/EventManager.ts", "line": 542, "severity": "medium", "category": "bug", "title": "Shared mutable credential variable across loop iterations may use wrong credential", "body": "In `updateAllCalendarEvents`, the variable `credential` is declared outside the for-loop (